WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:01.560
CARTER MORGAN:
Today, we're talking

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:04.050
about subsea cable,
startup, sustainability,

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:05.228
and monitoring your VMs.

00:00:05.228 --> 00:00:07.770
I'm Carter Morgan, and welcome
to "This Week in Cloud," where

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:10.830
we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:13.410
We're excited to announce
Apricot, a new subsea

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.810
cable that will connect
Singapore, Japan, Guam,

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:18.300
the Philippines,
Taiwan, and Indonesia.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:21.270
It's expected to be ready
for service in 2024.

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:24.300
In total, we have investments
in 18 subsea cables

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:28.170
alongside our 27 Cloud regions
in 82 zones around the world.

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:30.450
Check out the blog for more
about the subsea cables

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:32.180
and connectivity.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:34.580
Our first-ever Google
Cloud Startup Summit

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:37.640
will be taking place
on September 9, 2021.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:40.040
Google Cloud is committed to
maximizing your potential,

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.960
and we know how critical
mentoring and support

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:43.365
can be on a startup journey.

00:00:43.365 --> 00:00:45.740
We hope you will join us as
we bring together our startup

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:49.220
community, including startup
founders, CTOs, VCs, and Google

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:51.620
experts to provide
behind-the-scenes insights and

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:53.570
inspiring stories of innovation.

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:57.320
Check out the blog for a look at
the agenda and register today.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:59.240
A recent
Google-commissioned study

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:01.130
illustrated the importance
of sustainability

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:03.260
for organizations'
IT departments,

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:05.420
while also revealing
that significant work is

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:08.570
needed before businesses meet
their sustainability goals.

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:11.180
The good news is that 90%
say that sustainability

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:13.310
is a priority for
their IT departments.

00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:15.620
And as more organizations
consider the benefits

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:17.870
of digital transformation
and Cloud migration,

00:01:17.870 --> 00:01:20.780
sustainability is a must-have
or major consideration when

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.422
evaluating Cloud providers.

00:01:22.422 --> 00:01:24.380
Check out the blog to
learn about the obstacles

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:28.340
and pathways to progress and how
Google Cloud can be supportive.

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:30.440
We're happy to announce
the general availability

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:33.440
of an enhanced, in-context
set of UI-based tools

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:35.930
for Compute Engine users to
help make the troubleshooting

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:38.480
journey easier and
more intuitive.

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:40.010
From the Google
console, developers

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:42.290
can click into any VM
and access a rich set

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:44.930
of prebuilt visualizations
designed to give insights

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:48.680
into common scenarios and issues
associated with CPU, disk,

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:51.410
memory, networking,
and live processes.

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:53.420
With access to all of
this data in one location,

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:55.910
you can easily correlate between
signals over a given time

00:01:55.910 --> 00:01:56.660
frame.

00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:58.477
Check out the blog for more.

00:01:58.477 --> 00:02:00.560
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:02.487
or see the full list,
check out the link.

00:02:02.487 --> 00:02:04.070
And if you have any
thoughts or ideas,

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:05.690
leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:07.930
And we'll see you in the Cloud.

